# Done

Check this before saying finished. Every agent working here shares it, so
nobody gets to declare victory on their own terms.

**Done means zero outstanding issues in three places.**

## 1. Locally

- [ ] Installs from a clean checkout with the documented command
- [ ] Builds with no errors and no new warnings
- [ ] Starts, and the main flow can be completed by hand
- [ ] No errors in the log or the browser console during that flow
- [ ] Type check clean, lint clean

## 2. Tested

- [ ] Every test passes, not only the ones that passed before
- [ ] Coverage at or above {{COVERAGE_MIN}}%
- [ ] Every critical path in `docs/testing.md` has a test
- [ ] No test was skipped, weakened or deleted to get here

## 3. Deployed

- [ ] The same three local checks, against {{DEPLOY_TARGET}}
- [ ] Every environment variable set, and a missing one fails loudly at startup
- [ ] The main flow completes against the deployed instance

## A check you could not run

Record it as outstanding. Never skip it quietly.

```
Outstanding
  deployed check   not run: no deploy target configured yet
  coverage         71%, floor is {{COVERAGE_MIN}}%. Missing: {{GAPS}}
```

That block is the honest form of "not done".

## Fixing to zero

The loop is automatic: find, fix, verify, repeat. Two limits on it.

**It may not finish by deletion.** Removing the feature that fails, commenting
out the assertion, stubbing the endpoint: each reaches zero and none is a fix.
If a real fix needs a feature removed, that is a question for a person, and the
loop moves on to the next issue meanwhile.

**Nothing that worked before may work worse.** {{PARITY_BASELINE}}

If three full passes go by without the outstanding count dropping, stop and
report. A loop that is not converging will not converge.
